# Keeper environment names only. Supply values through the process environment or deployment env-file.
# Node startup does not implicitly load this file. Never commit populated credentials.
# Required at startup: KEEPER_INSTANCE, RPC_URLS.
# Sending modes additionally require SIGNER.
# KEEPER_PRIVATE_KEY is conditional on the local signer.
# AWS_KMS_KEY_ID is conditional on AWS KMS; GCP_KMS_KEY_NAME on GCP KMS.
# Cloud authentication should use an authorized workload identity where available.
# KEEPER_CONFIG, ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL, PORT and JOBS are optional runtime settings.
# Other names below belong to selected deployment, reporting or diagnostic commands.
# Uncomment only selected names; leave optional settings absent rather than empty.

# ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# AWS_KMS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_PROFILE=
# AWS_REGION=
# CYCLE_REPORT=
# FORK_RPC_URL=
# GCP_KMS_KEY_NAME=
# JOBS=
# KEEPER_ADDRESS=
# KEEPER_BASELINE_REPORT=
# KEEPER_CONFIG=
# KEEPER_CYCLE_REPORT=
# KEEPER_INSTANCE=
# KEEPER_PRIVATE_KEY=
# LOG_LEVEL=
# NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=
# PORT=
# RPC_URL=
# RPC_URLS=
# SIGNER=
# SOURCE_RPC_URL=
